## 8. Fundamental methodological rule

The Linux discussion must remain traceable as the **origin of the candidate reasoning**.

If later research establishes, modifies, rejects or replaces any of these candidates, the original source and this intermediate reasoning must remain preserved.

Therefore:

> **Source observation → interpretation → candidate principle → investigation → evidence → finding → possible governance**

must remain traceable.

No intermediate hypothesis becomes theory merely because it has survived brainstorming.
